      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "CallBackery versions before 0.62.0 for Perl allow OS command execution via sqlite3 shell commands in a restored configuration backup.\n\nrestoreConfigBlob() feeds the database dump in a backup to the sqlite3 command-line shell. The shell runs lines starting with a dot as its own commands, so .shell or .system in the dump runs an OS command and .load loads native code.\n\nAnyone who can supply a backup to be restored can run arbitrary commands as the application user.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
